<article class="env-corollary" id="039G">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/039G">Corollary <span data-tag="039G">9.2.1.13</span>.</a> Let $\lambda $ be an uncountable regular cardinal. Then $\infty $-category $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ admits $\lambda $-small filtered colimits if and only if it admits $\operatorname{N}_{\bullet }(A)$-indexed colimits, for every $\lambda $-small directed partially ordered set $(A, \leq )$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
<p>
<strong>Proof.</strong>
      Apply Proposition <a data-tag="062K" href="/tag/062K">9.2.1.11</a> in the special case $\kappa = \aleph _0$ (see Example <a data-tag="061Q" href="/tag/061Q">9.1.7.10</a>). 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
</p>
